# NetworkManager must not manage the interfaces omdrop-owl creates.
#
# The second line of defence behind 99-omdrop-owl-unmanaged.conf: udev's
# NM_UNMANAGED doesn't depend on how NetworkManager merges its conf.d, so it
# still holds if another file there changes what applies. Sorted after
# NetworkManager's own 85-nm-unmanaged.rules.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="net", KERNEL=="awdl0|mon0|awdlibss0", ENV{NM_UNMANAGED}="1"
